// The type-check project for the test suite (see issue #49).
//
// tsconfig.json is the BUILD project: rootDir "src", emit on, tests excluded. That
// contract is what `npm run build` needs, so it stays exactly as it is. The cost is
// that `npm run typecheck` compiles zero of the test files, and a test that imports a
// symbol which no longer exists passes both the compiler and Vitest (a missing export
// is `undefined` under the SSR transform, not an import-time throw). This project
// closes that gap: same strictness, rootDir at the repo root, emit off, tests in.
//
// noUncheckedIndexedAccess is off HERE and only here. Under it the suite reports 204
// errors, 115 of them index accesses like `text.split(' ')[0]` inside an assertion,
// where an undefined index throwing IS the check the test is making. Answering all 115
// with `!` would add noise without adding safety, and would make the flag mean
// something different in tests than it means in src. The remaining 89 were real enough
// to fix, and are fixed. src keeps the flag on: it compiles under tsconfig.json too,
// where the setting is inherited unchanged.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
